{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00538",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.14,
      "end_seconds": 10.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Good afternoon, come in. Did you manage to park all right? The lot was packed when I got in this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.3,
      "end_seconds": 20.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "Oh, don't ask, doctor. I went round three times. And this humidity, my shirt is sticking to me already."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.54,
      "end_seconds": 31.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "The monsoon is making everyone miserable. Sit down, make yourself comfortable. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.89,
      "end_seconds": 47.82,
      "duration_seconds": 14.93,
      "text": "It is my collarbone, doctor. I broke my collarbone three months ago, fell off my scooter on a wet road. They said it has healed, but I am still having pain in the collarbone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.21,
      "end_seconds": 53.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "I'm sorry to hear that. Tell me about the pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.66,
      "end_seconds": 68.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.9,
      "text": "It is a dull ache mostly, right on top of the bone. Sometimes sharp, like a pinch, when I lift my arm up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.92,
      "end_seconds": 79.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "The sharp pinch comes when you lift the arm. Anything else that sets it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.66,
      "end_seconds": 89.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Carrying my laptop bag on that shoulder. What to do, I have my files."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.73,
      "end_seconds": 97.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.18,
      "text": "So the bag and lifting the arm make it worse. Does anything help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.19,
      "end_seconds": 105.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "A hot water bag in the evening helps a little."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.35,
      "end_seconds": 112.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Mothers are often right. How bad is the pain on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.92,
      "end_seconds": 119.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Moderate, I would say. Not unbearable, but I notice it all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.8,
      "end_seconds": 126.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Okay. And the shoulder itself, does it move freely?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.07,
      "end_seconds": 137.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "There is a stiffness in the shoulder, mostly in the morning. It loosens up after I move around."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.55,
      "end_seconds": 145.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Morning stiffness that eases once you get going. Anything else you've noticed?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.59,
      "end_seconds": 157.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "Yes, there is a bump. A small bump right in the middle of the bone, which was not there earlier."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.9,
      "end_seconds": 167.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "I'll have a look at that shortly. Have you had any numbness in your fingers on that side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.31,
      "end_seconds": 177.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "No, no numbness. I can type, I can hold my cup, all normal on that front."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.13,
      "end_seconds": 184.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Good. And any pain in the neck as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.12,
      "end_seconds": 191.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "No, the neck is fine. It is only the collarbone area."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.67,
      "end_seconds": 203.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "That's very helpful. Now a few general questions. Any problems with breathing or a cough since the fall?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.33,
      "end_seconds": 206.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.5,
      "end_seconds": 213.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.88,
      "text": "Well done. Any longer-term health conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.95,
      "end_seconds": 221.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "Just the thyroid. I have an underactive thyroid, since about five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.19,
      "end_seconds": 227.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "And are you taking something for it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.23,
      "end_seconds": 234.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Yes, thyroxine, 50 micrograms every morning, on an empty stomach. My wife reminds me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.15,
      "end_seconds": 242.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "That's a clever reminder. And what work do you do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.23,
      "end_seconds": 254.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.82,
      "text": "I am an accountant, in a firm near the station. Desk work mostly, with lots of files going between offices."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.77,
      "end_seconds": 260.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "That explains the bag. Do you smoke at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.32,
      "end_seconds": 265.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "No, no, I have never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.25,
      "end_seconds": 281.13,
      "duration_seconds": 12.88,
      "text": "Good for you. Right, let me look at the shoulder. Could you take your shirt off on the left side, and I'll feel along the bone?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.72,
      "end_seconds": 285.66,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.25,
      "end_seconds": 311.25,
      "duration_seconds": 12.0,
      "text": "No problem at all. I can feel a firm, bony bump over the middle of the collarbone, and it's a little tender when I press."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.98,
      "end_seconds": 318.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Ouch. Yes, that is the sore spot. Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.08,
      "end_seconds": 340.72,
      "duration_seconds": 11.64,
      "text": "Let me finish looking. There's no redness and no warmth, so no sign of infection. Now lift your arm up slowly for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.17,
      "end_seconds": 349.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "It goes up, but there, there is the pinch again. At the top."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 351.66,
      "end_seconds": 360.74,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "I see that. The arm goes nearly all the way up, and the pinch is right where the bone healed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.63,
      "end_seconds": 368.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "So what is the bump? I thought the bone had joined wrongly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.7,
      "end_seconds": 386.95,
      "duration_seconds": 16.25,
      "text": "This is the usual thing. When a collarbone heals, the body lays down extra bone around the break, like a patch on a tyre. This looks like a healing callus, and the ache is the bone settling down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.93,
      "end_seconds": 392.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "A patch on a tyre. So it is a good thing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.37,
      "end_seconds": 406.22,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "It's the body doing its job. It may stay as a bump for months, and be a little tender while the bone remodels."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.43,
      "end_seconds": 412.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Okay, that is a relief. My wife was imagining the worst."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.89,
      "end_seconds": 427.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.11,
      "text": "So the key points: the bone has healed, the bump is extra healing bone, and the ache should fade over the coming months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.56,
      "end_seconds": 434.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Months? Doctor, can I do something about it meanwhile?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 436.57,
      "end_seconds": 449.45,
      "duration_seconds": 12.88,
      "text": "Keep up the hot water bag, that's a fine idea. And gentle shoulder stretches a few times a day will ease the morning stiffness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.05,
      "end_seconds": 454.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "What kind of stretches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.29,
      "end_seconds": 467.91,
      "duration_seconds": 12.62,
      "text": "Simple ones. Slowly circle the shoulder, then reach the arm forward and up as far as is comfortable. Ten times, morning and evening, no forcing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 470.33,
      "end_seconds": 476.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "That I can do, right after my tea. And the bag?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 477.73,
      "end_seconds": 489.31,
      "duration_seconds": 11.58,
      "text": "Switch to a rucksack with two straps so the weight is shared, and give the shoulder a rest from heavy loads for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 491.57,
      "end_seconds": 501.14,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "To repeat the main points: hot water bag, stretches, two straps, and the bump is just healing bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 502.53,
      "end_seconds": 509.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Yes, I have it. Thank you, doctor. I was really worried about nothing, it seems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 510.77,
      "end_seconds": 517.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.89,
      "text": "Not nothing, it was right to ask. Mind the wet floor on your way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 519.34,
      "end_seconds": 525.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "I will. Hopefully the rain stops before I find my scooter!"
    }
  ]
}
